# ------------------------------------------------------------------ generated

# Bytecode from the authoring tools in tools/ and
# assets/docs/buidling_to_voxel/ -- generated on whatever machine ran them.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# agent worktrees and local scratch
.claude/

# Private working notes: briefs written to an assistant, task prompts, local
# to-do. These carry absolute paths from the authoring machine (and with them
# a username), and they are notes to one person rather than documentation for
# anybody else. Kept on disk, kept out of the repository.
PROMPT_*.md
NOTES.md
TODO.local.md

# graphify's own output: a derived knowledge graph of this repo, rebuilt with
# `graphify . --code-only` whenever it is wanted. Nothing in it is source.
graphify-out/


# ------------------------------------------------ GAME DATA -- NEVER COMMIT
#
# This mod contains no Pokemon game data and must never start containing any.
# Gen1Recomp reads a ROM the player dumps from their own cartridge; this
# repository is Lua, generated art and documentation, and nothing else.
#
# A ROM PATCH IS NOT SAFE EITHER. A .bps / .ips / .ups file is a derivative of
# the copyrighted ROM it patches -- it is the diff of someone else's game --
# and publishing one is the most reliable way there is to get a fan project
# taken down. Patches used while working stay on the working machine.
#
# If you ever need to hand one to somebody, hand them a link to where its
# author published it, never the file.
*.gb
*.gbc
*.gba
*.nes
*.sfc
*.smc
*.nds
*.rom
*.bin
# Shipped mesh bakes (tools/optimize_*_glb.py). ROM dumps stay ignored.
!assets/ground/grass/grass.mesh.bin
!assets/ground/lamppost/lamppost.mesh.bin
*.bps
*.ips
*.ups
*.xdelta
assets/ground/source/*.zip
# Authoring-only GLBs (~20 MB); the bake is what ships.
assets/ground/grass/*.glb
assets/ground/lamppost/*.glb
# Same rule, and it had been missed: assets/mc/Mc.glb is 26 MB of source
# model. Nothing loads a GLB at runtime -- the bakes do -- so a clone that
# carried this would carry it forever for no one.
assets/mc/*.glb
publish-zip/
probe_out_atm/

# Save data: a player's own progress, and on some platforms their name.
*.sav
*.srm
*.sgm
*.rtc
*.state
*.state[0-9]
saves/
save/


# --------------------------------------------------------------- probe output
#
# The probes write to whatever DS_PROBE_DIR points at. When that is pointed
# inside the tree by accident, this keeps the screenshots and logs out of the
# history -- they are evidence for one run, not source.
#
# Common local conventions that previously leaked into git: a root folder
# named _probe_<run> (screenshots + console.txt + stdout/stderr) or DS_PROBE*.
# *.log alone is not enough -- PNGs and console captures were committed.
*.log
_probe_*/
DS_PROBE*/
probe-out/
probe_out/
tests/out/

# Captures written next to a driver when DS_PROBE_DIR is unset or mistyped.
# tests/*.lua drivers stay tracked; only runtime dumps under tests/ are blocked.
tests/**/console.txt
tests/**/stdout.txt
tests/**/stderr.txt
tests/**/*.png

# The legacy probe harness twenty-one dead probes used to load. It does not
# exist in this tree or in the build; listed so a stray copy is never
# committed as though it were the real one.
tests/drivers/


# ---------------------------------------------------------- heavy working art
#
# The generator's contact sheets the ground strips are recut from -- about
# nine megabytes of paper (see assets/ground/README.md). Already kept out of
# the packaged mod by .modkitignore, so this only matches that policy.
#
# DELETE THE LINE BELOW if you would rather a fresh clone be able to recut the
# ground art without asking you for the sheets.
assets/ground/source/*.png


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- OS junk
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*.swp
